issues.body:
Hi embeddedt,

I'm Joshua (Minecraft_2048 on CurseForge), and this is one of my first modding projects. Sorry for using an issue for a question; I couldn't find an email address.

I made an unofficial MinecraftForge port of ModernFix for Minecraft 26.2, which ModernFix doesn't ship builds for yet, and published it on CurseForge with credit, a link to your project, the LGPL-3.0 licence and the modified source code (https://github.com/Minecraft-2048/modernfix-forge). CurseForge moderation has since removed it, and I realise I should have asked you first.

Would you be OK with me publishing it again? If not, I will respect that.

If you agree, I commit to:
- a name and description that are clearly unofficial, crediting and linking ModernFix;
- the LGPL-3.0 licence kept, and the source code public;
- all bug reports directed to me, never to you;
- no monetisation, and no CurseForge rewards on the project;
- taking it down immediately if you ask, or as soon as an official 26.2 build exists.

Thank you for ModernFix.

Joshua

### Bug Description

If running the mod (versions intended for 1.16.4 and 1.16.5) with forge for version 1.16.4 it says that modernfix requiers version 1.16.5. since there is no version of the mod only for 1.16.4 you can't run it.

### Reproduction Steps

Just installed modernfix. Tried it with the latest version for 1.16.4/1.16.5 and three older versions. All the report. Look into the crash report I provided.

